                      (    forth6809.asm):06880         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):06881         ; TSTDEFWORDS - defining-words tests (glossary section 3.9, 17
                      (    forth6809.asm):06882         ; words, 12 tests since VALUE/TO and IS/ACTION-OF are each
                      (    forth6809.asm):06883         ; combined into one test). Every defining word parses a name
                      (    forth6809.asm):06884         ; from the input source via WORD (HEADER's own mechanism,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06885         ; shared by :/CREATE) - a complexity nothing in section 3.8 had.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06886         ; Each test redirects CODEHERE, DPHERE, VARHERE, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):06887         ; SRCADDR/SRCLEN/TOIN together (a fake name, "TESTWD", reused
                      (    forth6809.asm):06888         ; safely across every test here since each redirect/restore
                      (    forth6809.asm):06889         ; cycle is fully isolated), calls the real defining word
                      (    forth6809.asm):06890         ; directly, saves the newly-defined word's own CFA (= CODEHERE
                      (    forth6809.asm):06891         ; at the moment the defining word was called), restores
                      (    forth6809.asm):06892         ; everything, then executes that CFA directly to verify runtime
                      (    forth6809.asm):06893         ; behavior.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06894         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06895         ; A real, structurally important finding from this section:
                      (    forth6809.asm):06896         ; HEADER writes to the real LATEST variable unconditionally, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):06897         ; a redirectable copy like CODEHERE/DPHERE/VARHERE - every test
                      (    forth6809.asm):06898         ; here explicitly saves and restores it, confirmed necessary by
                      (    forth6809.asm):06899         ; reading HEADER's own code directly, not assumed safe by analogy
                      (    forth6809.asm):06900         ; with the other three pointers.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06901         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06902         ; MARKER's own test is the one exception to the general
                      (    forth6809.asm):06903         ; redirect-then-restore-then-execute order: DOMARKER (confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):06904         ; by reading it directly) writes to the real DPHERE/CODEHERE/
                      (    forth6809.asm):06905         ; VARHERE/LATEST unconditionally too, so that test executes the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06906         ; marker word while still redirected, only restoring the real
                      (    forth6809.asm):06907         ; environment afterward - getting this order backwards would
                      (    forth6809.asm):06908         ; have corrupted the real dictionary pointers with scratch
                      (    forth6809.asm):06909         ; addresses.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06910         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06911         ; Bare CREATE (never followed by DOES>) is deliberately not
                      (    forth6809.asm):06912         ; tested on its own - traced its placeholder "behavior field"
                      (    forth6809.asm):06913         ; (a genuine compiled JSR DOESRT0 instruction) and confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):06914         ; DODOES reads that field as raw data, not as code to execute -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06915         ; which only produces a valid jump target for the raw-address
                      (    forth6809.asm):06916         ; form every other defining word uses (VARIABLE, CONSTANT, etc,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06917         ; via CODECOMMA), not CREATE's own placeholder JSR instruction.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06918         ; Bare CREATE's own direct-execution behavior isn't meant to be
                      (    forth6809.asm):06919         ; relied upon before a DOES> patches it.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06920         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
C1F2 BDFC2B           (    forth6809.asm):06921         TSTDEFWORDS: JSR CRW
C1F5 8EC22A           (    forth6809.asm):06922                    LDX   #TSTDEFMSG
C1F8 3610             (    forth6809.asm):06923                    PSHU  X
C1FA CC0008           (    forth6809.asm):06924                    LDD   #8
C1FD 3606             (    forth6809.asm):06925                    PSHU  D
C1FF BDF60B           (    forth6809.asm):06926                    JSR   TYPE
C202 BDFC2B           (    forth6809.asm):06927                    JSR   CRW
                      (    forth6809.asm):06928         
                      (    forth6809.asm):06929                    IFEQ TSTSELECTOR-6  ; >>>>
                      (    forth6809.asm):06930         
