                      (    forth6809.asm):08235         ; TSTISOF - unit test for IS and ACTION-OF together. Compiles
                      (    forth6809.asm):08236         ; "DEFER TESTWD", interprets "DUP IS TESTWD" directly (IS parses
                      (    forth6809.asm):08237         ; "TESTWD" via WORD+FIND, needing LATEST still pointed at it -
                      (    forth6809.asm):08238         ; not restored until this whole test finishes), executes TESTWD
                      (    forth6809.asm):08239         ; (should now behave like DUP), then interprets "ACTION-OF
                      (    forth6809.asm):08240         ; TESTWD" to fetch the current target by name and confirms it
                      (    forth6809.asm):08241         ; matches DUP's own xt. Explicitly forces STATE=0 before both IS
                      (    forth6809.asm):08242         ; and ACTION-OF, since both are documented to behave differently
                      (    forth6809.asm):08243         ; by STATE, same reasoning as TSTVALTO's own TO test.
                      (    forth6809.asm):08244         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
