                      (    forth6809.asm):11757                                   ; EXIT's own EXITUNLOOP mechanism already
                      (    forth6809.asm):11758                                   ; discards the frame automatically and
                      (    forth6809.asm):11759                                   ; correctly on every path - traced and
                      (    forth6809.asm):11760                                   ; confirmed: with no enclosing DO (compiled
                      (    forth6809.asm):11761                                   ; count 0), with one enclosing DO and no
                      (    forth6809.asm):11762                                   ; prior UNLOOP (discards the full 8-byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):11763                                   ; frame correctly). The one combination that
                      (    forth6809.asm):11764                                   ; broke was UNLOOP immediately before EXIT -
                      (    forth6809.asm):11765                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):11766                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):11767                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):11768                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):11769                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):11770                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):11771                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):11772                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):11773                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):11774                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):11775                                   ; a second, conflicting discard mechanism.
