                      (    forth6809.asm):12921                                  ; file), so BPL was testing whatever flags an
                      (    forth6809.asm):12922                                  ; unrelated, earlier instruction happened to
                      (    forth6809.asm):12923                                  ; leave set, not the sign of the value just
                      (    forth6809.asm):12924                                  ; popped. TSTA explicitly tests D's high byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):12925                                  ; (bit 7 of A reflects the full 16-bit value's
                      (    forth6809.asm):12926                                  ; sign) immediately before the branch that
                      (    forth6809.asm):12927                                  ; depends on it. Confirmed via MAME debugger:
